SECOND, INDEPENDENT REPRODUCTION — dev, 2026-08-18 (task T-BRANDOPEN-0817)
================================================================================
The run above was not taken on trust. The pre-fix gate was recovered from git
(`git show HEAD:.proof-os/gates/F-0238-no-fabricated-contract-pdf.sh`) and run
against two scratch trees built from the REAL subject file:

  <scratch>/f0266/comment/  the real src/components/brand/deal-room/deal-contract-tab.tsx
                            plus THREE comment forms quoting the forbidden string:
                              const legacyToastRemoved = true; // used to read: "Opened a local copy"
                              {/* Historically this toast said "Opened a local copy" ... */}
                              /* block form: the retired copy was "Opened a local copy" */
                            No live code contains the string. This tree is CORRECT.

  <scratch>/f0266/code/     the same real file plus a genuine regression IN CODE:
                              export function Regressed() { toast.success("Opened a local copy"); }

OBSERVED, pre-fix gate:
    comment case (correct tree)   exit 1   "· the silent local-copy fallback message is still live in code"
    code case    (real regression) exit 1
    real repo tree                 exit 0

The gate cannot distinguish the two. It returns the same verdict for a correct
tree and a regressed one, so its exit 1 carries no information at all: it is
not "a gate that is sometimes wrong", it is a gate that is right by coincidence.
The real repo passes only because the one comment that quotes the string there
happens to start at column 0 with `//`, which the naive line filter did strip.

WHY THIS IS A DISEASE AND NOT A TYPO: the pressure it creates is to delete the
comment that explains the fix. Every producer who hits it learns to document
less. That is the opposite of what a trust layer is for.
